' 16. Battle and catch a wild kana (Kana Wilds)
' Use case: Battle a wild kana, «extend» Catch a kana (Play Kana Wilds) · Actor: Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Strategy: how an enemy attacks and how a defence is judged is picked per defence style from a map
'     (nihon-web/src/lib/kanaWilds/defenceStyles.ts ATTACK_PICKERS; wild kana use "reading")
'   - Facade: rewardActivity() hides XP, daily limits, achievements and level-up behind one call
'     (services/gamification.service.ts)
'   - Unit of work: a practice session and its streak day are saved together (practice-activity.service.ts)
'   - Observer: achievement / level-up notifications are published to every open tab (realtime.service.ts)
'   - Repository
' Where grading happens: each reading of an enemy attack is graded on the server (POST /api/quiz/answer, the same
' call kana quizzes use, so battles raise kana mastery). Damage, HP and the catch trace are worked out in the
' browser; the server only checks that a catch is allowed and saves it (docs/KANA-BATTLE.md section 11).
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens, «control» use-case logic, «entity» stored data; the database
' keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 16 Battle and catch a wild kana
title 16. Battle and catch a wild kana (Kana Wilds)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app\n(wild path)" as Web
control "Battle rules\n(defence style)" as Rules
control "Quiz controller" as Quiz
control "Activity controller" as Act
control "Kana Wilds controller\n+ service" as Wilds
control "Gamification\nservice" as Gam
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Notification\n(realtime)" as Notif

note over Web, Quiz : «Chain of responsibility»: headers → CORS → authenticate → controller\n«Decorator»: action() wraps every controller (error handling)
note over Repo : «Repository»\nall SQL lives here

Learner -> Web : Open a wild path
Web -> Wilds : GET /api/kana-wilds/collection
Wilds -> Repo : listCollection(), answers per kana, challenger wins
Repo -> DB : SELECT
Wilds --> Web : kana owned, answers, beaten challengers
Web -> Web : work out each kana's level (1–5) from its answers
Web -> Web : show the path, traveller at the arrival spot

loop each step
  Learner -> Web : Walk (arrow keys / WASD / touch)
  Web -> Web : move the traveller
  opt step onto tall grass (1 in 8, not in the 3 steps after a battle)
    Web -> Web : pick a wild kana from the path's rows\n(an uncaught one if any is left; otherwise an owned one, for practice, not catchable)
    Web -> Web : show the battle over the path
  end
end

loop until one side is worn out, or the learner runs
  Learner -> Web : Play a word from the hand
  Web -> Web : word's power from its kana levels → damage, show the hit

  Web -> Rules : pickAttack("reading", enemy, words)
  note right of Rules : «Strategy»\none picker per defence style\n(reading, look-alikes, shout, …)
  Rules --> Web : the kana or word it attacks with
  Web -> Web : draw the attack stroke by stroke, show the choices
  Learner -> Web : Choose the reading
  Web -> Quiz : POST /api/quiz/answer (kana, answer, submissionId)
  Quiz -> Repo : grade + save the answer (same submissionId never counts twice)
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE kana progress
  Quiz --> Web : correct? + right answer
  Web -> Web : block / perfect block / hit, show the result

  opt enemy at or below 60% HP
    Learner -> Web : Catch it! (chance shown)
    Learner -> Web : Trace the kana's strokes
    Web -> Web : check stroke order, direction and shape, roll the chance

    alt caught
      Web -> Wilds : POST /api/kana-wilds/catches { kanaId }
      Wilds -> Repo : starter chosen? row open? (さ/た rows need Chun, ま… need Tama)
      alt not allowed
        Wilds --> Web : 409 with the reason
        Web -> Web : show the reason
      else allowed
        Wilds -> Repo : addCaughtKana()
        Repo -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
        opt first catch of this kana
          Wilds -> Gam : rewardActivity("game", "kana-wilds-catch:<id>")
          note right of Gam : «Facade»\nXP (daily game limit) +\nachievements + level
          Gam -> Repo : award XP, check achievements
          opt new achievement / level up
            Gam -> Notif : notify
            Notif -> DB : save notification
            Notif -> Web : publish → bell updates (all open tabs)
            note right of Notif : «Observer»
          end
          Gam --> Wilds : reward
        end
        Wilds --> Web : collection + isNew + reward
        Web -> Web : show "Caught!" and "+XP", the kana joins the collection
      end
    else trace missed or it broke out
      Web -> Web : the kana attacks; after 3 failures it runs away
    end
  end
end

opt at least 3 readings answered
  Web -> Act : POST /api/activity/practice { kind: "battle", answered, correct }
  Act -> Act : validate (kind, numbers, 60 sessions an hour)
  group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
    Act -> Repo : insertPracticeSession() + recordActivity() (streak day)
    Repo -> DB : INSERT / UPDATE
  end
  Act -> Gam : rewardActivity("game", "session:<id>")
  Gam --> Act : reward (daily game limit)
  Act --> Web : recorded, streak, reward
  Web -> Web : show "+XP"
end
Web -> Web : close the battle, traveller back on the same tile
@enduml
